From: znyrvalt <220587351+znyrvalt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 07:22:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] AltarSMP 2.0.5: Bedrock/Geyser crossplay, restored
 ability artwork, model-data fixes

Model-data reconciliation (all values trace to the plugin sources in
Altar_SMPS1-2-sources-FRESH.jar or to the pack's own range_dispatch files):

- content catalogue now agrees with the pack on every entry: 60 entries carry
  custom_model_data (armor 8, items 22, weapons_s1 24, weapons_s2 6)
- CopperPickaxe regains plugin truth (NETHERITE_PICKAXE, cmd 1, its display
  name) - the same visual/slot as CopperPickaxeII, as the plugin stamped them
- CopperFragment, CopperChestplateFragment, IllusionCore, FragmentOfTheSea get
  reserved discriminators on materials the pack does not dispatch
- CopperDiamondArmor pieces get cmd 1, the copper appearance their lore promises
- Omen moves to DIAMOND_SPEAR (the plugin's own preference; mace:1 was a
  dangling threshold) and Bow of Deception gets reserved BOW 0
- gradle.properties: mod_version 2.0.5

Restored ability artwork: the 192 tooltip sprites under
assets/altarsmp/textures/gui/sprites/tooltip/** are committed in the mod's own
resources again, byte-for-byte from AltarSMP-ResourcePack.zip.

First-pass crossplay package AltarSMP-Custom-Content/: Geyser custom-item
mapping (format_version 2 legacy definitions on custom_model_data), Bedrock
resource pack (manifest, item definitions, item_texture.json, icons, ability
tooltip artwork) and the full Java->Bedrock inventory. Weapon icons are still
source textures - the next commit rebuilds the package with a real renderer.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
